    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39961" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quaestūra</span></b> , ae, f.
		quaestor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the office of quæstor</i>, <i>the quæstorship</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quaestura primus gradus honoris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Verr. 1, 4, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quaesturam petere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Mur. 8, 18</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 3, 29</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex quaesturā consulatum petere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					32, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gerere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 1</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>the
				quæstor</i>'<i>s chest</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">translator quaesturae,</span>”
				<i>an embezzler of the public chest</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 5, 58, § 152</span></i>
			.</div>
